{
  "duration": 69.839,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.179,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.959,
      "end": 3.5,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.039,
      "end": 8.26,
      "text": "Now let us first read the question. A floating log moves at four kilometer per hour"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.76,
      "end": 9.3,
      "text": "with the current."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.719,
      "end": 12.259,
      "text": "A boat has still water speed twelve kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.899,
      "end": 14.899,
      "text": "We need to find the boat's upstream speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.319,
      "end": 15.639,
      "text": "Given,"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.119,
      "end": 18.879,
      "text": "speed of the floating log equals four kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.379,
      "end": 22.6,
      "text": "Boat's speed in still water equals twelve kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.019,
      "end": 26.559,
      "text": "Let B equals speed of the boat in still water,"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.079,
      "end": 28.719,
      "text": "C equals speed of the current."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.039,
      "end": 29.26,
      "text": "Here,"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.859,
      "end": 32.059,
      "text": "B equals twelve kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.419,
      "end": 33.939,
      "text": "Now we need to find the value of C."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.419,
      "end": 36.799,
      "text": "A floating log has no engine of its own."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.319,
      "end": 39.54,
      "text": "It simply moves with the flowing water."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.079,
      "end": 43.419,
      "text": "So the speed of the floating log is always equal to the speed of the current."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.86,
      "end": 44.219,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 44.779,
      "end": 49.34,
      "text": "C equals four kilometers per hour. Now, when a boat moves upstream, it moves against the current."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.879,
      "end": 51.839,
      "text": "The current slows the boat down."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.299,
      "end": 55.019,
      "text": "So upstream speed equals B minus C."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.539,
      "end": 56.799,
      "text": "Now substitute the values."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.259,
      "end": 62.5,
      "text": "Upstream speed equals twelve minus four. Upstream speed equals eight kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.199,
      "end": 67.059,
      "text": "Hence, the boat's upstream speed is eight kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.5,
      "end": 69.839,
      "text": "So the correct option is option A."
    }
  ],
